# One set of line endings on every machine.
#
# The project is worked on from a Mac and a Windows PC. Without this file, Git
# for Windows checks text files out with CRLF endings: the shell scripts in
# tools/ then fail in Git Bash, and test data that is compared byte for byte
# differs between the two machines.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows command files are the exception: cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Never treated as text, whatever their content looks like.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.bin binary
*.jar binary
*.onnx binary
*.keystore binary
*.ico binary
*.icns binary
